      "message": "Based on the naming I would expect the same thing, but FWIU, `static_libs` in `android_library_imports` are not actually static in that they don\u0027t even end up in the the `classes.dex` (at least they\u0027re not in the input JAR (e.g. Settings.jar) which causes the warning in the first place, nor even referenced in [the r8 command](https://paste.googleplex.com/5787845569544192)).\n\nMy understanding so far is that `android_library_imports` also don\u0027t run r8, so they\u0027re always included as deps for some other module (which may run r8), and for the reason above its deps will be `libs` dependencies rather than `static_libs`.\n\nTbf, I\u0027m very surprised that something called `static_libs` wouldn\u0027t be in the APK at least, so I\u0027ll look a little more to see if I find anything else.\n\nI never understood the naming of the `androidx` imports (e.g. [`androidx.mediarouter_mediarouter-nodeps`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:prebuilts/sdk/current/androidx/Android.bp;l\u003d4094-4134;drc\u003d106df7bb07a145cf7c739c7cdae4bdfad8fb9e4b)) with `-nodeps` counterparts for everything, but it does make more sense now in light of what I found above.",
